Root cause: The Radios component only updates ARIA attributes and conditional visibility on click events, not on keyboard-driven changes (arrow keys). So when user changes selection via keyboard, the conditional content remains visible.

Repair strategy: Add a change event listener that triggers the same update logic as click, ensuring ARIA attributes and visibility are updated for all radios when selection changes via any interaction (including keyboard).

Expected accessibility effect: Keyboard navigation will now correctly show/hide conditional fields when selecting different radio options, meeting WCAG 2.1.1 (Keyboard) and 2.4.3 (Focus Order) and 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value).

Functional risks: Potential duplicate handling if both click and change fire for mouse clicks (may cause double updates but idempotent). Risk of interfering with other custom handlers if they rely on change event; but unlikely. Also ensure that change event does not cause infinite loops.

Verification requirements: Verify that arrow key navigation between radios hides/shows appropriate conditionals; verify that mouse click still works; verify that form data reflects correct value; verify that ARIA attributes aria-expanded and visibility of conditionals update accordingly.

